WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Open the local Streamlit app

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Choose Guest for temporary JSON storage, or create a Browser profile to remember separate history on this browser

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Select System, Light, or Dark appearance.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Study the supported prior-probability correction experiment

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Name the conditions and a measurable prediction

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Include a competing hypothesis, rather than asking an unrestricted research question.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Set experiment and token budgets

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Reserve independent confirmation seeds before exploration

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Review the execution settings and choose an installed model on your Ollama-compatible server.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Inspect measured results, decisions and event logs

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
LazyLoop may reuse an exact verified result while allowing independent replications

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Stop run pauses the worker; Resume investigation continues a nonterminal checkpoint.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.750
A budget stop does not confirm a hypothesis

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.500
In Provenance and export, prepare a portable ZIP bundle

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.250
In Guest mode, Open research bundle restores saved history

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.000
Review imported settings before resuming.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Configure a reachable Ollama-compatible HTTP or HTTPS base URL and discover installed models

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Inference may be remote; experiments and files stay on the app host

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Learn and help includes the research lesson and practice questions.
